0..74 Comment "// Cases over the circle its loop refuses, and one it admits that looks as"
75..151 Comment "// though it should not. A case over the circle owes its loop: carried along"
152..229 Comment "// the loop, its answer at the point must be that answer, by conversion or by"
230..303 Comment "// a loop arm at the path between the two. Last, two operations on paths,"
304..368 Comment "// written with no path type stated, that their operands refuse."
